<h1>Todos</h1>

<p class="muted">
  The relational custom-database demo: <code>todos</code> plus
  <code>todoImages</code>, whose <code>todo</code> field is a relation back.
  Reads come from the data-model API; the create goes through the generated form.
</p>

<form method="post" action={~p"/todos"}>
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={get_csrf_token()} />
  <input type="text" name="title" required placeholder="What needs doing?" />
  <input type="text" name="notes" placeholder="Notes (optional)" />
  <button type="submit">Add</button>
</form>

<ul :if={@todos != []} class="todos">
  <li :for={todo <- @todos}>
    <strong>{get_in(todo, ["fields", "title"])}</strong>
    <span :if={get_in(todo, ["fields", "done"])} class="done">done</span>
    <p class="muted">{get_in(todo, ["fields", "notes"])}</p>
    <img
      :for={image <- Map.get(@images_by_todo, todo["id"], [])}
      src={get_in(image, ["fields", "url"])}
      alt=""
      width="120"
    />
  </li>
</ul>

<p :if={@todos == []} class="muted">
  <span :if={@configured}>
    No todos yet. Run <code>npm run sync-data-model</code>, promote the model in
    the dashboard, then set the generated "Todo Form" Live.
  </span>
  <span :if={not @configured}>
    Connect this app to a BD site to see live records.
  </span>
</p>
